<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/7th-century-bce">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of Carchemish</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">605 BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/7th-century-bce">7th century BCE</a> · Also known as Carchemish</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of Carchemish was fought in 605 BCE at Carchemish on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/euphrates">Euphrates</a>. The Babylonian crown prince <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nebuchadnezzar-ii">Nebuchadnezzar</a> defeated the Egyptian army and the remnants of Assyrian forces. The victory gave the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chaldean-empire">Chaldean Empire</a> control of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/syria">Syria</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/levant">Levant</a>; Carchemish itself had earlier been a major centre of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hittite-empire">Hittite Empire</a> and its successors.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-carchemish.jpg" alt="Battle of Carchemish" width="320" height="228" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Egisto C. · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:The_Battle_of_Carchemish.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>The <b>Battle of Carchemish</b> in 605 BCE, won by the crown prince Nebuchadnezzar II against the Egyptian army of Pharaoh Necho II, secured the Levant and turned a regional kingdom into the dominant power of the ancient Near East.</blockquote><a href="/empire/chaldean-empire">Chaldean Empire · Foundation</a></li><li><blockquote>After Nebuchadnezzar II defeated the Egyptians at the <b>Battle of Carchemish</b> in 605 BCE, Jehoiakim submitted to Babylon but later rebelled.</blockquote><a href="/empire/kingdom-of-judah">Kingdom of Judah · Decline &amp; Fall</a></li></ul></section>
